.TH "WINDOW.DOCUMENTPICTUREINPICTURE" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Window.documentPictureInPicture \- Window: documentPictureInPicture
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]documentPictureInPicture\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of
the \f[CR]Window\f[R] interface returns a reference to the
\f[CR]DocumentPictureInPicture\f[R] object for the current document
context.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]DocumentPictureInPicture\f[R] object instance.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] videoPlayer = document.getElementById(\(dqplayer\(dq);

\f[I]// \&...\f[R]

\f[I]// Open a Picture\-in\-Picture window.\f[R]
\f[B]await\f[R] window.documentPictureInPicture.requestWindow({
  width: videoPlayer.clientWidth,
  height: videoPlayer.clientHeight,
});

\f[I]// \&...\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Document Picture\-in\-Picture API
.IP \(bu 2
Using the Document Picture\-in\-Picture API
